## 6. Test Schedule / Milestone
- Test Design & Environment Prep: 2 days
- Script Development & Mock Setup: 2 days
- Execution & Results Analysis: 2 days
- Total Duration: 6 days
- Resources: 1 QA Automation Engineer, 1 Test Lead

## 7. Assumptions
- Test environments have stable connectivity to Jira API or mocks.
- Test credentials for all required permutations are available.
- Testers have access to logs and error traces.

## 8. Quality Objectives
- Validate API authentication and permissions.
- Verify error handling for missing or inaccessible Jira issue descriptions.

## 9. Risk Mitigation Table
Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation Action
---|---|---|---|---
R1 | Dynamic Jira API connectivity failures | High | Medium | Use mock/stub services for 401 and null description scenarios.
R2 | Test credential matrix incomplete | Medium | Medium | Pre-seed all credential types and validate before execution.
R3 | Ambiguous error messages (e.g., 'null - null') | High | High | Enhance log capture and assert on error message content.
R4 | Timeline slippage due to environment setup | Medium | Medium | Parallelize environment prep and mock configuration.
R5 | Inaccessible Jira description field | High | High | Focus only on authentication/error handling until access is restored.

## 10. Tools Table
Tool | Purpose
---|---
Playwright | UI error rendering and validation
PyTest | API and integration test automation
JMeter | SLA and error response simulation
OWASP ZAP | Security/authentication validation
tcconfig | Network condition simulation
